TITLE:: SnapCommand
SUMMARY:: Command that snaps notes to the nearest grid line defined by a musical resolution.
CATEGORIES:: Commands
RELATED:: Classes/Command, Classes/Parameter, Classes/CommandPrompt, Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/PianoRollNote

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::SnapCommand:: is a LINK::Classes/Command:: that snaps an LINK::Classes/Array:: of notes (e.g. from LINK::Classes/PianoRoll#*selectedNotes::) to the nearest beat subdivision.

It accepts a positive integer CODE::resolution:: between 1 and 16, representing the fraction of a beat (1/N beats):
LIST::
## CODE::1::: Whole beat (every 1.0 beat, matching the vertical beat lines)
## CODE::2::: Half beat (every 0.5 beats)
## CODE::4::: Quarter beat (every 0.25 beats)
## CODE::8::: Eighth beat (every 0.125 beats)
## CODE::16::: Sixteenth beat (every 0.0625 beats)
::

Each note's start time is shifted in the closest direction to the nearest multiple of CODE::1.0 / resolution:: beats while preserving duration.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new TELETYPE::SnapCommand::.

ARGUMENT:: action
An optional callback LINK::Classes/Function:: evaluated after note snapping completes. Receives the arguments LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: containing CODE::\selectedNotes:: and CODE::\resolution::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::SnapCommand:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
(
var note = PianoRollNote(1.2, 60, 100,
	viewFunc: { View() },
	selectFunc: {},
	deselectFunc: {},
	setPart1Func: {},
	setPart2Func: {},
	setPart3Func: {},
	setPart4Func: {},
	moveFunc: { |view, start, stop| ("Moved to " ++ start ++ ".." ++ stop).postln; }
);
note.stop(2.2);

var snapCmd = SnapCommand({
	|args|
	("Snapped note to start: " ++ note.startTime).postln;
});

// Snap to nearest quarter note (resolution = 4)
snapCmd.execute((
	selectedNotes: [note],
	resolution: 4
));
)
::
